WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.553
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Focus Fuel Gauge.

00:00:14.553 --> 00:00:21.107
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.107 --> 00:00:25.039
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:28.971
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:28.971 --> 00:00:38.145
Inside you, there is a kind of gauge. It does not measure gas. It measures your focus — how much attention you have for the work in front of you.

00:00:38.145 --> 00:00:48.631
The gauge has three easy readings. Full: your mind feels ready and bright. Half: it is working, but it drifts. Low: everything feels like pushing through mud.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:01:00.427
Every gauge moves during the day. Full in the morning, low after lunch, back up again. That is not a problem. That is just how gauges are.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:05.670
And here is the important part: your gauge belongs to you. Nobody else can read it. Let me show you how to read it yourself.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:17.466
Checking takes three quiet seconds. Ask inside: where is my needle right now? Full, half, or low? Whatever it says is fine. It is just a reading.

00:01:17.466 --> 00:01:29.262
If the reading is low, your job is not to push harder. Your job is to refill — a little, in an ordinary way.

00:01:29.262 --> 00:01:41.058
A sip of water. A slow stretch in your chair. A quiet minute with soft eyes. One deep breath, in and out. Looking far away, out the window, to rest your eyes.

00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:51.543
Small refills. Ordinary refills. The kind anybody is allowed to take, any day, without asking the gauge to explain itself.

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:52.854
Then check again. Not to grade it — just to notice. The needle moves. That is what needles do.

00:01:52.854 --> 00:02:04.650
Hear this clearly: a low reading is not bad, and a full reading is not good. They are just readings.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:16.446
Needing a refill is never a failure. It is maintenance — the same way a bike needs air and a plant needs water. Nobody is behind because their gauge is low.

00:02:16.446 --> 00:02:25.621
And your gauge is private. You never report it. Nobody lines the gauges up to compare. The check happens inside, where only you can see it.

00:02:25.621 --> 00:02:26.931
Grown-ups have gauges, too. Theirs move all day, just like yours.

00:02:26.931 --> 00:02:36.106
Check the needle. Pick a refill. That is the whole job.

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:42.660
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.902
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:47.902 --> 00:02:54.456
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:54.456 --> 00:03:01.009
You're ready for what's next.
